    "description": "The combination of devastating US air strikes and the economic pain of Hormuz closure creates pressure on both sides. Iran's remaining leadership — with C2 severely degraded and military capacity collapsing — signals through Omani back-channels a willingness to accept a ceasefire framework. Trump, facing the April 6 energy-strike deadline and rising US gasoline prices, finds a face-saving off-ramp. The air campaign tapers to occasional enforcement strikes by mid-April. Houthis are pressured by the Saudis to halt attacks. Hezbollah, already weakened from the 2024 war, scales back. The conflict enters a 'frozen' state — no formal peace deal, but active combat largely ends within 6-8 weeks of the February 28 start. The critical question becomes how fast Hormuz can be reopened once hostilities cease.",
